)
(text "Lofrans load is 3.3 V / 47k = 70 uA, and only while the shunt is on pins 1-2. The 4.7k pull-up is on DRY_A and cannot reach REED_SIG in that position.\\nR20 is 10k in series. D20 and D21 clamp LOFRANS_NODE to the field 3.3 V rail. The Lofrans wire is not connected to an ESP32 pin.\\nMEJ2S0303SC is 3.3 V to 3.3 V. R24 is 51 ohm, about 65 mA, just over 10 percent of the 606 mA rating, so the published load envelope applies.\\nMurata: hipot 5.2 kVDC for 1 s, continuous functional barrier 2.4 kVDC. Not a safety barrier. The LCSC YLPTEC listing is not this part.\\nBlanker: ISO7720F outputs go low when the field side is unpowered. Q_NPG makes NOT_PG. The diode-OR and the two NAND gates are an SR latch.\\n/S is PG, so a field-supply loss sets BLOCKED and Q_BLK holds REED_GPIO low. That is a falling edge, which the existing firmware does not count.\\nThe latch clears only when PG is high and REED_DATA is low, which is the start of a real pulse. The following rise is the end of that pulse.\\nSupply loss and recovery while idle produce no counted rising edge. Recovery during a real pulse counts that pulse once or misses it.\\nUntil the first real pulse after power-up, REED_GPIO is held low. The firmware samples that level and does not treat the sample as an edge.\\nINB is tied to the field rail, so OUTB is high only while the isolator considers that rail valid. This is not a separate precision supervisor." (at 20 40 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))) (uuid "c6d5a33e-77ce-4b11-afa0-4c591ce423d3"))
  (embedded_fonts no)
)
